-# Encrypted folder creation API (UC23)
+# Encrypted folder API
+
+## Create an encrypted folder (UC23)
 
 `POST /api/folders` creates an owned folder from client-encrypted content. Send a current Heimdall bearer token and one `X-Cerberus-Vault-Access` header. Responses use `Cache-Control: no-store`.
 
 The body requires `folderId`, `envelope`, `editedAt` and `profileIds`. `parentFolderId` may be omitted or null for a root. Public IDs use canonical lowercase UUIDs; profile IDs must be unique and nonzero. A folder cannot be its own parent. The envelope uses `cerberus-content-v1` with initial key epoch 1. The encrypted name remains a client-side requirement; the API neither receives nor validates a plaintext name.
 
 `editedAt` must be UTC and at least `0001-01-01T00:00:00.000001Z`. The server floors it to microseconds before persistence. Success is 201 with `folder_created` and exactly `folderId`, `revision`, `serverSequence` and `editedAt`; the initial revision is 1. Internal database IDs, access credentials and encrypted parent/profile content are absent from this output.
 
 Account-wide access can create an unlinked root or associate the new folder with multiple owned active profiles. Selected access requires exactly that selected profile in `profileIds`. An optional parent must already be visible through owned direct folder ancestry or an active owned collection attached to the selection. A read/write collection grant does not allow creating folders for another owner. Parent and all ancestors must remain active, nonterminal and in the same account.
 
 Creation inserts the folder and direct profile links atomically. Each directly linked profile and the immediate parent advances its structural revision/server sequence once; existing ciphertext, key wrappers, client edit times and other links remain intact. Ancestors and selections reached only through inheritance do not receive fabricated direct changes. A failed transaction leaves none of these changes behind.
 
 The server rejects malformed/unknown/duplicate/case-variant body fields, invalid envelopes, self-parent input, compressed/non-UTF-8/BOM bodies, query parameters and malformed/repeated access headers with 400. Oversized input gets the common empty 413. Missing identity or access is 401; current revoked, expired or superseded access is 403. Hidden/missing/foreign/trashed/terminal relationships are nonrevealing 404. A folder UUID already present, trashed or permanently reserved, or exhausted affected revision capacity, yields 409. Necessary corrupt structural state or unavailable persistence yields 503. Known failures return no success payload.
 
 Folder identifiers are reserved within the folder kind. A record, profile, account, collection or grant marker using the same UUID cannot block a distinct folder. Retrying a lost successful creation returns 409 rather than duplicating links or metadata. Reload the winning state before retrying a conflict.
 
 New folders belong to the complete owned protection-rotation inventory. Missing a folder rejects rotation before proof consumption; complete rotation preserves its client edit time, parent and links. A record can use a newly created permitted folder immediately. Offline inherited visibility delivery and external-client key provisioning remain release qualification obligations.
+
+## List encrypted folders (UC24)
+
+`GET /api/folders` returns a page of currently permitted active folders. Send the current Heimdall bearer and one `X-Cerberus-Vault-Access` header, including for an empty result. Success is 200 with `folders_found`; `data` contains exactly `items` and nullable `nextCursor`. Each item contains exactly `folderId`, `revision`, `serverSequence`, `editedAt` and `envelope`. Content remains opaque; no parent, owner, profile, collection, grant, internal ID or key wrapper is returned. Detailed visible relationships belong to the folder lookup use case.
+
+Account-wide scope includes owned folders and current native read-only/read-write collection member folders and their descendants. Selected scope includes owned direct folder associations and descendants, plus member folders of currently selected owned or granted collections. Overlapping associations appear once. A record-only collection grant or direct profile-record association does not expose the containing folder. A member leaf does not expose its otherwise unshared parent, ancestors or siblings.
+
+Ownership, current profile/access policy, active grants, typed terminal markers and trash exclusion apply before pagination. Every candidate must have complete active same-owner ancestry. Hidden or incomplete ancestry omits the candidate before grant inspection; a fully active relevant cycle fails 503. Unselected/ungranted corrupt hierarchy cannot turn unrelated folder listing into an availability oracle. All contributing visible foreign grants are validated against their collection, epoch, grant revision, recipient identity and owner/recipient native pins, including overlapping and nonpage contributors. A corrupt relevant contribution fails the entire response without partial content. Pins and native grant envelopes remain internal.
+
+Only optional exact-case `pageSize` and `cursor` are accepted. Page size is canonical positive decimal, at most configured `MaxPageSize`; default is the smaller of 50 and that limit. Reject repeated/unknown/case-changed keys, signs, whitespace, leading zeros, nonintegers, overflows, malformed/empty cursors, repeated/malformed access headers and GET bodies, including unknown-length bodies. Shared oversized-body rejection returns an empty 413. All responses are no-store.
+
+The initial page captures the largest visible server sequence as its high-water boundary; subsequent pages include only greater sequences up to that boundary. Newly created or changed folders with later sequences are excluded from that continuation. The authenticated encrypted folder-specific cursor binds actor, hashed handle, page size, position and boundary. Record/profile cursors, actor/handle/page-size substitutions, tampering and changed cursor-key configuration reject with 400. Restart after key rotation. Current permissions are rechecked on every page, so removals can shrink or empty a continuation. This list is not durable synchronization or an immutable content snapshot.
+
+One SQL statement captures current authority, complete relevant ancestry, ordering, page and native evidence using database statement time. A grant revoked after this snapshot takes effect on the next call. Listing writes no content, associations, access state or structural metadata. Nonpositive/unsafe/duplicate ordering in the visible inventory fails before keyset filtering; invalid public IDs, counters, UTC microsecond timestamps or supported native envelope metadata in the returned page fail without partial output.
+
+Visible malformed input is 400; missing identity/handle is 401; revoked, expired, superseded or hidden selected access is 403; missing/inactive/terminal account is 404. Hidden folders are omitted. Necessary persisted/native corruption or unavailable persistence is 503. The shared OpenAPI requiredness/nullability and empty-413 metadata findings remain release follow-ups. Independent security/protocol and external-client key provisioning/decryption/operability qualification remain deferred for development only; this endpoint does not imply release approval.
